 To force a textfield in Adobe to display columns, you can use the TextFrame's `textFlow` property and create a `Paragraph` object with multiple `TextLine` objects. Each `TextLine` can represent a column. Here's a simple example:

```javascript
// Assuming you have a TextField named "myTextField"
var textField = myTextField;

// Create a new TextFlow
var textFlow = new TextFlow();

// Create a Paragraph and add multiple TextLine objects to it
var paragraph = new Paragraph();
var column1 = new TextLine("Column 1 content");
var column2 = new TextLine("Column 2 content");
paragraph.addChild(column1);
paragraph.addChild(column2);

// Set the width for each column
