 In LaTeX, you can create a new line within a cell by using the `\\` command. Here's a simple example of a LaTeX table with a cell containing multiple lines:

```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{tabularx}

\begin{document}

\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{|X|}
\hline
\textbf{Cell with Multiple Lines} \\
\hline
This is the first line. \\
This is the second line. \\
This is the third line. \\
\hline
\end{tabularx}

\end{document}

```

In this example, the `\\` command is used to create new lines within the cell. The `tabularx` package is used to create a table that spans the width of the text area. If you want to create a table with multiple columns, you can adjust the number of `X` in the `tabularx` environment to match the number of columns you need.

